CORE
main.c
--arrays-uf-always --no-propagation --no-simplify
^\[main.assertion.1\] .* equal indices, equal elements: SUCCESS$
^\[main.assertion.2\] .* element written by a with: SUCCESS$
^\[main.assertion.3\] .* equal indices of a leaf: SUCCESS$
^\[main.assertion.4\] .* different indices may differ: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Ackermann constraints i=j => a[i]=a[j] are only added to arrays whose
constraints do not follow from those of other arrays: the constraints for
with, if and equalities must then relate elements at all indices.
